toward the city, by which the Achaeans, dazed with fear, had fled
on the day before, when raged glorious Hector;

And as before a dolphin, huge, the other fish
fleeing fill the inner nooks of a harbour of good anchorage,
fearing; for exceedingly it devours whichever it catches;

And he, when he grew weary in his hands slaying,
alive from the river twelve picked out, youths,
as requital for Patroclus, Menoetius’ son, who was dead;

Him then, as he noticed, swift-footed, heavenly Achilles,
naked, without helmet and shield, nor did he hold a spear,
but those things all away on the ground he had thrown;

He then, for his part, a long spear held up, heavenly Achilles,
eager to wound, and he ran in under and took hold of his knees,
stooping;

